From 680443d236cb2a3b995a1947494998750d6c4577 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ymakarovskaya <y.makarovskaya@axis.moscow>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:48:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Lead each old hotel.thefah.com page to its section of /en/fah

hotel.thefah.com was the hotel's own English site (2016-2021). Instead of
sending every old address to the top of https://axis-hotels.com/en/fah,
two maps keep the meaning of each archived page: rooms and galleries go
to #fah-rooms or the room's own card, facilities to #fah-hotel, contacts
to #fah-contacts, offers to the FAH booking page, /ru and /th paths to
/ru/fah and /th/fah, and anything else to /en/fah as before.

The playbook additionally checks six old pages over HTTP and HTTPS
before it keeps the change, so a wrong section triggers the existing
rollback. Unit tests cover every archived address; a new isolated
real-Nginx check runs them against the rendered virtual hosts in CI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
